I get off the U-Bahn.
On the way home, I go into the supermarket.
Today I quickly shop for dinner.
First I take a shopping basket.
The vegetables are right at the entrance.
I look for fresh vegetables.
I take tomatoes and a zucchini.
Then I go to the next shelf.
I still need a packet of pasta.
I put the pasta in the basket.
After that, I go to the till.
I put my things on the belt.
The cashier scans the vegetables and the pasta.
"That comes to four euros eighty," she says.
I pay with my card.
"Do you need the till receipt?" she asks.
"No, thank you," I answer.
I pack my groceries into the backpack.
Then I walk the rest of the way home.
